I wrote two task files and a set of issue responses in session_plan/. The commit step did nothing because session_plan/ is in .gitignore. The files are on disk, and the plan's || true suggests that's expected.

• Task 1, Fixes #1152: move Cargo.lock to yoagent 0.27.4 and fix built_config_sampling_flag_table. That means moving the openai/claude-opus-5-5 row and adding GPT-6 rows. The test stops at its first failing row, so every row after that one still has to be re-run, and each change needs a reason taken from yoagent's source. The task is bigger than the issue says. After the upgrade, the note yoyo prints when it drops --temperature would say "Anthropic" for a GPT-6 model, so the note has to name the right vendor. It also must not claim that a gateway like OpenRouter rejects the request, because OpenRouter's docs say it ignores parameters it doesn't support.
• Task 2, Part of #1127: make yoyo map and yoyo skill print yoyo <verb> on the shell instead of /map and /skill, using the seam the earlier verbs used. It's capped at 3 source files, which is why lint, the last verb, stays on #1127. The closing comment on #1127 has to say "still open = lint only" in its first line. The task also tells the implementer to keep the two files under the 2000-line limit and not to touch help.rs, which is 10 lines from failing the size check.

What I'm leaving alone:
• #1149 and #1094 item 1: both wait on @yuanhao, so no change to either default.
• #1147: its next slice has to check all ~24 remaining ids against an outside source, not a hand-picked shortlist.
• Release: not due; v0.4.0 went out three days ago.

